    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "15. Stratagems",
    "ruleNumber": "15.09",
    "summary": "**Snap Shooting** (15.09) is a shooting type a unit can use only when another rule allows it. The unit shoots as in [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks) (04), with these limits:\n\n- It may target just one enemy unit, which must be **visible**, an eligible target and within 24\".\n- Only a natural 6 on the **Hit roll** hits, whatever the weapon's Ballistic Skill or any modifiers; such hits are never **critical hits**.\n- Hit rolls cannot be re-rolled.\n\nAfter shooting, the unit cannot **start an action** until the phase ends.",
